---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';

const person = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: SITE.author,
  url: new URL('/about/', SITE.url).toString(),
  jobTitle: 'Music producer and designer',
  knowsAbout: ['Music production', 'Ableton Live', 'Psytrance', 'Home recording', 'Audio interfaces', 'MIDI controllers'],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Ophir"
  description="Who's behind HomeStudioEquipment: Ophir, a psytrance producer, Ableton user, and designer who sums up owner reviews of home studio gear in plain English."
  jsonLd={[person]}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About HomeStudioEquipment</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Hi, I'm Ophir. I'm a music producer and a designer. This site sums up what real owners say about home
      studio gear, so you can decide faster.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes these reviews?</h2>
    <p>
      I produce psytrance in Ableton Live, so I spend a lot of time with audio interfaces, MIDI keyboards, pad
      controllers, and monitors. <!-- TODO: add your story: how long you've produced, releases/labels, current setup. -->
    </p>

    <h2>How do we choose and review gear?</h2>
    <p>
      We read owner reviews on Amazon, both positive and negative, and summarize the patterns: what owners like, what
      they complain about, and who the product seems to suit. Specs come from the manufacturer. Unless a post says
      otherwise, we haven't tested the product ourselves. Everything is written in our own words. We never copy
      customer reviews and we never show prices that go out of date. Instead, we link you to the current price on
      Amazon. Read more about <a href="/how-we-review/">how we review</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How does this site make money?</h2>
    <p>
      Some links are Amazon affiliate links. If you buy through them, we earn a small commission at no extra cost
      to you. It never changes what we recommend. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>
      for details.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
